# [variant] Issue #104 (item 3): the QEMU build with comprehensive heap poisoning, applied after
# sdkconfig.qemu (and sdkconfig.qemu-psram). Freed memory is filled with 0xFE and every block
# carries canaries checked when it is freed: a use after free reads garbage instead of the old
# value (the issue #98 check of the cut download then fails on the old code) and an overrun
# aborts. tools/e2e/run_e2e.sh with E2E_POISON=1 (build dir build-qemu-poison, or
# build-qemu-psram-poison). It costs memory on every allocation and time on every malloc and
# free: docs/reference/e2e-harness.md#heap-poisoning has its effect on the #80 margins. Never flash this build.
CONFIG_HEAP_POISONING_COMPREHENSIVE=y
